.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/

# Local working notes for coding agents. Deliberately untracked — they are a
# personal scratchpad, and duplicating the status block into the repo is the
# drift the handoff warns about.
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md

# graphify-out/ is a regenerable index of the source tree, not a collection.
# It is not an AD graph and must never be cited as one.
graphify-out/

# Coursework tooling. Builds the Review-1 report from templates under
# ~/Downloads, so it hardcodes absolute paths and runs for nobody else. Kept on
# disk, out of the repo. `tools/_*` catches the .docx dumps it unpacks.
tools/build_review1_report.py
tools/_*

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Research artifacts: kept on disk, out of the repo (2026-09-27)
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The repo ships the app. These back the parked write-up rather than the
# running tool, and they are most of its weight.
#
# `data/goad_graph.json` is NOT here and must not be: it is the collection the
# app demos on and every reported number cites by hash. Re-collecting would
# silently change the substrate under results already generated.
#
# Tests that need one of these skip rather than fail, so a fresh clone is green
# and pytest reports the skip count. Restoring any of them is one `git add -f`.
data/goad_graph_perturbed.json
data/raw_collection/
results/figures/

# Research write-up. The app-facing docs (handoff, scope_minimum) stay tracked.
docs/abstract.md
docs/findings.md
docs/generator_vs_real_distribution.md
docs/stage0_hypotheses.md
docs/stage0_related_work.md
docs/stage1_lab_runbook.md
docs/stage2_joint_capability_audit.md
docs/stage3_risk_model_properties.md

# Screenshots of a superseded dashboard layout. Removed rather than kept stale.
docs/screenshots/
